      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While resting can sometimes help with migraines, the extremely sudden onset of severe pain is still something that should be monitored closely. If the pain does not significantly decrease or if new symptoms develop, you must seek medical care immediately. If you decide to wait, monitor for any changes like fever, stiff neck, or neurological changes, and be ready to go to the ER if those occur. When in doubt with sudden, severe headache, professional medical advice is the safest choice.",
